---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE, FAQS } from '../consts';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Main from '../layouts/Main.astro';
import Hero from '../components/HowToPlay/Hero.astro';
import StartingHandImage from '../assets/starting-hand.png';
import DraftBoard from '../assets/draft-board.jpg';
import AaronePastim from '../assets/aarone-pastim.png';
import HughFitt from '../assets/hugh-fitt.png';
import PassPlusOne from '../assets/pass+1.png';
import PassMinusTwo from '../assets/pass-2.png';
import GoalsArea from '../assets/goals-area.png';
import CardHappy from '../assets/card-happy.png';
import Varcical from '../assets/varcical.png';

const faqSchema = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "FAQPage",
	"mainEntity": FAQS.map((faq) => ({
		"@type": "Question",
		"name": faq.question,
		"acceptedAnswer": {
			"@type": "Answer",
			"text": faq.answer
		}
	}))
};
---
<style>
    section.content {
		width: 100%;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 20px;
		position: relative;
		display: none;
	}

	section#game-modes {
		display: block;
	}

    .section-heading {
        position: relative; 
        z-index: 2;
        font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif;
        font-size: 30px;
        text-align: left;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em; 
        line-height: 0.95;
        margin: 20px 0;
        animation: fadeUp 0.7s 0.25s ease both;
		color: var(--lime);
    }

	section.content h3, section.content p strong {
		color: var(--lime);
    }

    section.content p {
        padding: 10px 0;
    }

	section.content ul, section.content ol {
		margin: 10px 0 10px 24px;
	}

	section.content li {
		padding: 4px 0;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	section.content li strong {
		color: var(--lime);
	}

	.outcomes {
		display: grid;
		gap: 16px;
		margin: 10px 0 20px;
	}

	@media (min-width: 800px) {
		.outcomes { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
	}

	.outcome {
		background-color: var(--navy-mid);
		border-left: 3px solid var(--lime);
		border-radius: 4px;
		padding: 16px 20px;
	}

	.outcome h4 {
		font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif;
		font-size: 1.6rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.04em;
		color: var(--white);
	}

	.outcome ul {
		margin-left: 18px;
	}

    section.content a {
        color: var(--lime);
        text-decoration: none;
    }

    section.content a:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
    }

	img.draft-board {
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
	}

	.mini-nav {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: row;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: flex-start;
		gap: 20px;
		margin: 20px 0;
		padding: 0 20px;
		width: 100%;
		overflow-x: scroll;
	}

	.mini-nav div[role=button] {
		cursor: pointer;
		padding: 10px 20px;
		background-color: var(--navy-mid);
		border-radius: 4px;
		transition: background-color 0.3s;
		text-align: center;
		text-wrap: nowrap;
	}
	.mini-nav div[role=button]:hover {
		background-color: var(--navy-dark);
	}

	.mini-nav div[role=button].active {
		background-color: var(--lime);
		color: var(--navy-dark);
	}

	.example {
		background-color: var(--slate);
		padding: 20px;
		margin: 10px 0;
	}

	.example .example-title {
        font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif;
        font-size: 30px;
        text-align: left;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em; 
        line-height: 0.95;
        margin-bottom: 10px;
		color: var(--lime);
	}

	.example-images {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: row;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: flex-start;
		gap: 10px;
		margin-top: 20px;
		max-width: 100%;
	}

	.example-images.duel img {
		height: 100px;
		width: auto;
	}

	.example-images.chaos img {
		height: 200px;
		width: auto;
	}

	img.goals-area, img.starting-squad {
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
	}

	@media (min-width: 800px) {
		.example-images {
			gap: 20px;
		}
		.example-images.duel img {
			height: 200px;
			width: auto;
		}
		img.goals-area {
			height: 100px;
			width: auto;
		}
		img.starting-squad {
			height: 200px;
			width: auto;
		}
	}
	@media (min-width: 1080px) {
		.mini-nav {
			overflow-x: hidden;
		}
	}
</style>
<script type="text/javascript">
	function onMiniNavClick(id) {
		window.scrollTo({
			top: document.getElementById("mini-nav").offsetTop - 120,
			behavior: 'smooth'
		});

		setTimeout(() => {
			document.querySelectorAll('.mini-nav div[role=button]').forEach(button => {
				button.classList.remove('active');
			});
			document.getElementById(id + '-button').classList.add('active');

			document.querySelectorAll('section.content').forEach(section => {
				section.style.display = 'none';
			});
			document.getElementById(id).style.display = 'block';
		}, 200);
	}

</script>
<Main title="How to Play Totally Football | Rules & Quick Start Guide" description="Learn how to play Totally Football, the tactical football board game, in minutes: pick your squad, win duels across three pitch zones and use chaos cards to score." includeDiscoverMore={true} includeJoinTheSquad={true}>

	<Hero />

	<div id="mini-nav" class="mini-nav">
		<div id="game-modes-button" class="active" role="button" onClick="onMiniNavClick('game-modes');">Game modes</div>
		<div id="setup-button" role="button" onClick="onMiniNavClick('setup');">Setup</div>
		<div id="the-draft-button" role="button" onClick="onMiniNavClick('the-draft');">The draft</div>
		<div id="match-day-button" role="button" onClick="onMiniNavClick('match-day');">Match day</div>
		<div id="match-duels-button" role="button" onClick="onMiniNavClick('match-duels');">Match duels</div>
		<div id="chaos-cards-button" role="button" onClick="onMiniNavClick('chaos-cards');">Chaos cards</div>
		<div id="added-time-button" role="button" onClick="onMiniNavClick('added-time');">Added time &amp; penalties</div>
	</div>

	<section id="game-modes" class="content">
		<p>First, decide on a competition format. Choose your game mode, agree on a playing order, then move on to setup and pre-season. As a guide, each match takes <strong>20–30 minutes</strong>, depending on your experience and playing style.</p>

		<h3>Head-to-Head (2 players)</h3>
		<p>Play a set number of matches against your opponent. Always use an odd number to allow an outright winner. Our recommended starting format is a <strong>best-of-three</strong>.</p>

		<h3>League (3–4 players)</h3>
		<p>Everyone plays each other once, or twice for a longer season. You might choose to play a League over multiple sessions.</p>
		<p><strong>3 points</strong> for a win, <strong>1 point</strong> for a draw. The person with the most points wins.</p>

		<h3>Knockout (3–4 players)</h3>
		<p>Everyone rolls a dice to complete the draw:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>3 players:</strong> the lowest two rolls play each other. The highest roll gets a bye and then plays the winner.</li>
			<li><strong>4 players:</strong> the highest roll plays the lowest, and the second-highest plays the third.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Win and advance. Lose and you're out. Can you be the last team standing?</p>

		<div class="example">
			<div class="example-title">Good to know</div>
			<p>In 3–4 player games, anyone not involved in a match can try to influence events on the pitch from the sidelines by using their Chaos Cards.</p>
			<p>Matches can be played simultaneously if you have <strong>two</strong> game boards.</p>
		</div>

		<p>
			<div class="btn-primary" onClick="onMiniNavClick('setup');">Setup ></div>
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="setup" class="content">
		<h3>Game setup</h3>
		<p>Place the game board in the middle of the table. Shuffle each deck of cards (<strong>Goalkeepers</strong>, <strong>Squad Players</strong>, <strong>Star Players</strong>, <strong>Action Cards</strong> and <strong>Chaos Cards</strong>) and place them in their spaces on the board.</p>
		<p>The two people playing a match sit on opposite sides of the board (top and bottom). The view of the pitch is the same from each side.</p>

		<h3>Pre-season: deal your squad</h3>
		<p>Each of you draws <strong>eight</strong> Player Cards. You can draw from the <strong>Squad Player</strong> and <strong>Goalkeeper</strong> decks, with a maximum of <strong>two</strong> Goalkeepers. Keep all eight and lay them face-up in front of you, next to the board.</p>

		<p>Each of you also draws <strong>four</strong> Chaos Cards. Keep these secret in your hand. After each match, they're topped back up to four.</p>

		<Image class="starting-squad" src={StartingHandImage} alt="A starting hand: six Squad Player cards, two Goalkeeper cards and four Chaos Cards" />

		<div class="example">
			<div class="example-title">Quicker games</div>
			<p>For quicker games, or for younger players (12 and under), you can skip the Chaos Cards.</p>
		</div>

		<p>Then it's time to strengthen your squad with some stars.</p>

		<p>
			<div class="btn-primary" onClick="onMiniNavClick('the-draft');">The draft ></div>
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="the-draft" class="content">
		<h3>Draft your Star Players</h3>
		<p>Shuffle the Star Player deck and deal <strong>eight</strong> cards face-up into the spaces on the game board.</p>
		<p>Roll the dice to decide the draft order: the highest roll picks first. Take turns choosing a Star Player to add to your squad until every card on the board has been drafted.</p>

		<Image class="draft-board" src={DraftBoard} alt="Eight Star Player cards dealt face-up onto the Totally Football game board for the draft" />

		<p>Star Players have better stats and will boost your squad. Lay them face-up in front of you, next to your other Player Cards.</p>

		<h3>3 and 4 player games</h3>
		<p>Reload the board for a <strong>second draft</strong>, so that everyone adds <strong>four</strong> Star Players to their squad. <strong>Reverse</strong> the draft order for the second draft.</p>
		<p>In a 3 player game, only place <strong>six</strong> Star Players on the board for each draft, so everyone drafts four cards.</p>

		<p>Once the draft is done, you'll each have a squad of <strong>twelve</strong> Player Cards.</p>

		<div class="example">
			<div class="example-title">Fantasy Football draft</div>
			<p>If you really enjoy squad building, why not try a fantasy football style draft?</p>
			<ol>
				<li>Set a budget for each person's squad. <strong>£400m</strong> is a good starting budget. Adjust it to make the draft easier or harder.</li>
				<li>Load the board with <strong>3 Star Players</strong>, <strong>4 Squad Players</strong> and <strong>1 Goalkeeper</strong>.</li>
				<li>Draft in rounds until everyone has a squad of <strong>twelve</strong> or more Player Cards. Pick any Player Card you can afford and keep track of your budget. If you've overspent, reload the board and swap Player Cards until you've balanced the books.</li>
			</ol>
			<p>A player's value is only needed for the Fantasy Football draft, but it's also a useful guide to how good they are.</p>
		</div>

		<p>Before you start the draft, read your Chaos Cards: some of them can be used in pre-season.</p>

		<p>
			<div class="btn-primary" onClick="onMiniNavClick('match-day');">Match day ></div>
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="match-day" class="content">
		<p>Time for kick-off! Each match is played over <strong>two halves</strong>. A half lasts as long as it takes for both of you to use <strong>five</strong> Action Cards.</p>

		<h3>Warm-up</h3>
		<ul>
			<li>Place all your Player Cards face-up next to the board.</li>
			<li>Each person playing the match is dealt <strong>ten</strong> Action Cards. Choose <strong>five</strong> to use in the first half and set the other five aside, face-down, for the second half. Keep your Action and Chaos Cards in your hand, away from your opponent.</li>
			<li>Choose a Goalkeeper for the match and place them in goal, on the left side of the pitch on <strong>your</strong> side of the board. You can choose any of your Player Cards to play in goal, even if they aren't a Goalkeeper. That might be necessary after a Goalkeeper injury.</li>
			<li>Each of you rolls the dice. The highest number starts the first half with possession of the ball. The opponent starts the second half with the ball. Re-roll ties.</li>
		</ul>

		<h3>First half</h3>
		<p>Play <a href="#mini-nav" onClick="onMiniNavClick('match-duels');">duels</a> until both of you have used all <strong>five</strong> of your first-half Action Cards. Then play one <a href="#mini-nav" onClick="onMiniNavClick('added-time');">Added Time</a> duel.</p>

		<h3>Second half</h3>
		<p>The other team starts the second half with the ball. Play duels until both of you have used all <strong>five</strong> second-half Action Cards, then play one more Added Time duel.</p>

		<h3>Full-time</h3>
		<p>Whoever has scored the most goals after two halves wins the match.</p>
		<p>Tied matches in a Knockout or Head-to-Head competition go to a <a href="#mini-nav" onClick="onMiniNavClick('added-time');">penalty shootout</a>.</p>

		<h3>The three zones</h3>
		<p>Each match is a series of duels across the pitch. As you win and lose duels, the ball token moves between Player Cards around three zones. You can only score when you have the ball token.</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Build-up:</strong> new attacks begin here at the start of each half, straight after a goal, or when your Player Card wins possession in this zone.</li>
			<li><strong>Progression:</strong> you attack from here after a successful pass or dribble out of the build-up zone, or when you win possession with a Player Card in this zone.</li>
			<li><strong>Final third:</strong> once you reach the final third, your only option is to shoot. Duels here are always against your opponent's Goalkeeper.</li>
		</ul>

		<h3>Scoring</h3>
		<p>Place a goal token in your goals area after every goal, and during a penalty shootout.</p>
		<Image class="goals-area" src={GoalsArea} alt="The goals area on the game board, with goal tokens"  />

		<p>Player Cards that have been used in a duel go to your <strong>Used Players</strong> space on the board. They return to your squad when the match ends.</p>

		<p>
			<div class="btn-primary" onClick="onMiniNavClick('match-duels');">Match duels ></div>
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="match-duels" class="content">
		<p>A duel is a battle between a Player Card from each team, to move the ball up the pitch, score a goal or win possession. Action Cards boost your players' stats or harm your opponent's.</p>

		<h3>1. Choose your attacker</h3>
		<p>The attacking team places a Player Card face-up in the active zone and puts the ball token on it.</p>

		<h3>2. Declare your action</h3>
		<p>The attacking team chooses an action:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Pass:</strong> moves the ball to a <em>new</em> Player Card further up the pitch.</li>
			<li><strong>Dribble:</strong> moves <em>this</em> Player Card, with the ball, further up the pitch.</li>
			<li><strong>Shoot:</strong> an attempt to score a goal.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Long passes and long shots (see below) must be declared at this stage.</p>

		<h3>3. Defending team chooses a player</h3>
		<p>The defending team chooses a Player Card and places it face-up across from the attacker, in the same vertical zone on the opposite side of the board. If the attacker <strong>shoots</strong>, the defending team's Goalkeeper takes the duel instead.</p>

		<h3>4. Choose Action Cards</h3>
		<p>You each choose an Action Card in secret and reveal them at the same time. You <strong>must</strong> play an Action Card, even if it won't affect the duel. Used Action Cards are discarded once the duel is over.</p>

		<h3>5. Compare stats</h3>
		<p>The defending stat is never chosen. It's always the opposite of the attacking action:</p>
		<p>
			Shooting <strong>vs</strong> Saving<br />
			Passing <strong>vs</strong> Intercepting<br />
			Dribbling <strong>vs</strong> Tackling
		</p>
		<p>Add the Action Card modifiers to the Player Card stats to get a total for each player. Positive Action Cards boost stats and negative ones reduce them. Action Cards only affect the actions involved in the duel, so a card might help or hurt your own player, help or hurt your opponent's, or do nothing at all.</p>
		<p>If the totals are tied, the <strong>defending</strong> Player Card wins the duel.</p>

		<div class="example">
			<div class="example-title">Example</div>
			<p>The attacking team is passing with a passing stat of 5. The defending team's chosen player has an intercepting stat of 5.</p>
			<p>The attacker plays a +1 Pass Action Card. The defender plays a -2 Pass Action Card against them.</p>
			<p>The attacking total is 4 (5 + 1 - 2).</p>
			<p>The defending total is 5, because neither Action Card affected intercepting.</p>
			<p>So, the defender wins.</p>
			<div class="example-images duel">
				<Image src={PassPlusOne} alt="+1 Pass Action Card" />
				<Image src={AaronePastim} alt="Aarone Pastim, passing 5" />
				<p><strong>vs</strong></p>
				<Image src={HughFitt} alt="Hugh Fitt, intercepting 5" />
				<Image src={PassMinusTwo} alt="-2 Pass Action Card" />
			</div>
		</div>

		<h3>What happens next</h3>
		<div class="outcomes">
			<div class="outcome">
				<h4>If the attacker wins</h4>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Pass:</strong> both Player Cards are discarded. The attacking team places a new Player Card in the next zone up the pitch and begins a new attack. Long passes from the build-up zone go straight to the final third.</li>
					<li><strong>Dribble:</strong> the defending Player Card is discarded. The attacking Player Card moves into the next zone with the ball and begins a new attack.</li>
					<li><strong>Shoot:</strong> GOAL! The attacking team adds a goal token and their Player Card is discarded. The defending team takes the ball and attacks from their build-up zone with a new Player Card. The Goalkeeper stays in goal.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="outcome">
				<h4>If the defender wins</h4>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Pass or dribble:</strong> the attacking Player Card is discarded. The defending team takes the ball and attacks from their current zone with the Player Card that won the duel.</li>
					<li><strong>Shoot:</strong> saved! The attacking Player Card is discarded. The defending team takes the ball and attacks from their build-up zone with a new Player Card. The Goalkeeper stays in goal.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h3>Long passes and long shots</h3>
		<p>You can attempt a long pass or a long shot, but you must declare it at stage 2.</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Long pass:</strong> moves the ball from the build-up zone straight to the final third, with <strong>-1</strong> to your passing stat.</li>
			<li><strong>Long shot:</strong> your shooting stat gets <strong>-2</strong> from the build-up zone, or <strong>-1</strong> from the progression zone.</li>
		</ul>

		<p>
			<div class="btn-primary" onClick="onMiniNavClick('chaos-cards');">Chaos cards ></div>
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="chaos-cards" class="content">
		<p>You'll receive <strong>four</strong> Chaos Cards at the start of the game. Chaos Cards can be played at different moments, but each of you can only play <strong>three</strong> during a single match. Cards used before a match count towards this, and you <em>can</em> use all three before a match begins.</p>
		<p>At the start of each match, new Chaos Cards are dealt so everyone has <strong>four</strong> in their hand. Any unused cards from the previous match stay in your hand.</p>

		<h3>Three things to remember</h3>
		<ol>
			<li>Each person can only use <strong>one</strong> Chaos Card during a duel, with a maximum of <strong>two</strong> cards allowed in a duel.</li>
			<li>Chaos Cards can be played at different moments: <strong>pre-season</strong>, <strong>before or after a match</strong>, and <strong>before, during or after a duel</strong>. Each card explains when it can be used.</li>
			<li>In 3 and 4 player games, those not involved in a match can use up to <strong>two</strong> Chaos Cards per match to interfere with play. Their cards are topped back up to four before they play their own match.</li>
		</ol>

		<p>To use a card, place it face-up on the table and <strong>call out the chaos</strong>. The first person to lay down a card has priority, but each Chaos Card must be completed before a second one can be played.</p>
		<p>Chaos Cards don't just affect events on the pitch. They let you steal Player Cards from other teams, change your Action Cards and injure Player Cards before matches. So be sure to read your Chaos Cards before you begin the draft.</p>

		<div class="example">
			<div class="example-title">Example</div>
			<p>The attacking team plays a “Card Happy” Chaos Card: the defending player is sent off, so the attacking team wins the duel.</p>
			<p>The defending team reacts by playing a “VARcical” Chaos Card to cancel the red card. The initial duel result stands.</p>
			<div class="example-images chaos">
				<Image src={CardHappy} alt="Card Happy Chaos Card" />
				<p><strong>vs</strong></p>
				<Image src={Varcical} alt="VARcical Chaos Card" />
			</div>
		</div>

		<p>
			<div class="btn-primary" onClick="onMiniNavClick('added-time');">Added time &amp; penalties ></div>
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="added-time" class="content">
		<h3>Added time</h3>
		<p>After five duels with Action Cards in each half, whoever has the ball has a final chance to score from whichever zone they're in. If the previous duel ended in a goal or a save, the team now in possession shoots from their build-up zone with a new Player Card.</p>
		<p>The defending player in an Added Time duel is always the Goalkeeper.</p>
		<p>Instead of using Action Cards, each of you rolls the dice and adds the value to the matching “shoot” or “save” stat to decide the duel. Chaos Cards can still be used during added time.</p>

		<div class="example">
			<div class="example-title">Ties</div>
			<p>Tied duels are won by the <strong>defending</strong> Player Card. During added time and penalties, <strong>Goalkeepers</strong> win tied duels.</p>
		</div>

		<h3>Penalty kicks</h3>
		<p>Chaos Cards can award you a penalty kick during normal time. If so, choose a Player Card and place it in the final third for a duel against your opponent's Goalkeeper. Each of you rolls the dice and adds the value to the matching “shoot” or “save” stat.</p>
		<p>If it's a goal, add a goal token to your goals area. Goal or save, the defending team then restarts with a new Player Card in their build-up zone.</p>

		<h3>Penalty shootout</h3>
		<p>In Head-to-Head and Knockout competitions, tied matches are decided by the thing every football fan dreads: a <strong>penalty shootout</strong>. Time to bite your nails and hide behind the sofa.</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Arrange your squad of Player Cards into a single face-up deck, in the order you want them to take penalties.</li>
			<li>Both Goalkeepers stay in goal and face every penalty in the shootout.</li>
			<li>Take turns to place a Player Card in your final third and play a penalty duel with the dice.</li>
			<li>Place a goal token in your goals area: ball side up for a goal, “X” side up for a miss.</li>
			<li>Take <strong>five</strong> penalties each. If it's still tied, move on to <strong>sudden death</strong> until one of you scores and the other misses.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>
</Main>
